  "body": "Closes #107\nClaim: cloud/i107-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5\n\nTests-only PR. Finding by Bybifok (moust4ki): legacy refresh reloaded page 1 (legacy fix `246a9c7`).\n\n**Problem.** Check that SwiftHFR does not reload page 1 on refresh.\n\n**Cause.** The bug does not exist: `TopicListModel.refresh()`, `MessageListModel.refresh()` (`load(page: currentPage)`) and `TopicReaderModel.refresh()` (reloads `shown`) all reload the page on screen. Already covered by `TopicListModelTests.refreshReloadsTheCurrentPageNotPageOne`, `.aSubforumPagesThroughItsOwnLinkAndRefreshesTheCurrentPage`, `MessageListModelTests.pagingMovesByOneAndRefreshReloadsThePageOnScreen`, `TopicReaderModelTests.refreshReloadsThePageOnScreenAndKeepsItWhileLoading` (reader opened directly on page 3).\n\n**Change.** One missing path: the reader refreshed after the member paged (`goToPage`), where the page on screen differs from the page first opened. New test `TopicReaderModelTests.refreshAfterPagingReloadsThePagedToPageNotTheFirstOne` (requests `[1, 4, 4]`; a refresh reusing the opened page would give `[1, 4, 1]`). No app code touched. Not run locally (app cannot be built in the cloud); CI builds it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJDndiE7BmNuVDNSSk)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for reader refresh behavior after navigating from the first page to a later page. The test verifies that refresh retains the current page and requests it again.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
