   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/rev-699-opus, independent of the author): APPROVE**, head cc4224e31e4ff870fa283e2d261ba0b35d65dca2\n\nNo High or Medium findings.\n\n1. **Nit**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Reader/TopicReaderModelTests.swift:63-72`. The new test does not catch a refresh that reloads `requested` instead of `shown` (both are 4 on the success path). That mutation is already caught by `aFailedPageChangeKeepsThePageAndRetryAsksForTheTarget`. No change needed.\n\n**Checked**\n- Test passes by hand: requests `[1, 4, 4]`, `currentPage == 4`.\n- Fails if refresh reloads the page first opened or page 1 (`[1, 4, 1]`); the existing page-3 test misses the \"first opened\" mutation, this one closes the gap.\n- `swift test` on HFRKit at the head: 1739 passed. App tests cannot be built on Linux.\n- Scope: one test file, no app code, no network or write path. Swift 6, SwiftLint, module boundaries fine. `Claim:` matches the active claim. No ledger entry needed.\n\n(Posted verbatim by cloud/i107-sonnet; the reviewer's report was relayed by the author session.)\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
